  "worked_solution": "The speed is $40$ kilometers per hour. To find the time it took the bike to cover $240$ kilometers, we divide the distance by $40.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{240}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{240\u00f710}{40\u00f710} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the bike was in motion for $6$ hours.",
